    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "As spring weather improved travel conditions, a rise in encounters with people in need was recorded, with apprehensions increasing along the southwest border. Despite this statistical trend, the current policy framework of asylum shutdowns and deportation measures continues to limit access to protection for vulnerable migrants. The ongoing legislative dispute among those responsible for funding care has created a political stalemate, leaving federal law enforcement without the resources to adequately address the humanitarian situation.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Caregiver",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "result-0",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.88
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Seasonal change brought more people facing the risks of the journey, resulting in a numerical increase in apprehensions for the border security agency in March. This border activity metric highlights the challenges faced by those at risk during crossing. Meanwhile, elected officials remain deadlocked, creating a government impasse over funding for immigration enforcement agencies. The failure to provide resources for protection exacerbates the vulnerability of apprehended individuals caught in a system strained by a funding dispute.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Caregiver",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.82
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "With the arrival of spring weather, enforcement personnel saw an increase in apprehensions from February to March, a clear immigration statistic reflecting heightened border activity. Observers of the situation note that this numerical change occurs under policies that limit access to protection, an enforcement policy outcome that leaves many detainees in precarious situations. The political deadlock among government officials prevents the allocation of necessary support, leaving those responsible for funding care to neglect their duty to the affected population.",
      "source": {
